<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-rŏgo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To ask through in succession</i>, <i>to ask one after another</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sententias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					29, 19</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac.
				H. 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug.
			35</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to carry
			through</i>, <i>to pass</i> (a law) after proposing
			it: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tribunus plebis legem perrogavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 8, 6, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">1, 2</span></i> ext.
		1.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
